          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "barato comes from an old verb for trading and selling low, whose own origin is uncertain. Old French barater, behind English barter, belongs to the same family."
            }
